WEBVTT

00:42.676 --> 00:46.013
Hey, man, I think it's about
time we haul it up out of here.

00:46.046 --> 00:48.015
Yeah, might be.

00:48.048 --> 00:50.851
Let me finish this first.

00:53.687 --> 00:56.690
It's a nice night, though.

00:56.724 --> 00:58.359
It's quiet.

00:58.392 --> 01:00.528
A little too quiet.

01:00.561 --> 01:03.697
This place always gave me
the heebie-jeebies, man.

01:03.731 --> 01:06.867
This water's so murky.

01:06.900 --> 01:08.569
It's shit water.

01:09.537 --> 01:12.039
I almost drowned in it once
when I was like eight.

01:12.072 --> 01:15.209
Actually, right over there
by the beach.

01:15.243 --> 01:17.211
My cousin had to drag me out.

01:18.212 --> 01:20.548
I don't know what it was, man.

01:20.548 --> 01:23.317
I just felt like
I was being pulled.

01:25.052 --> 01:27.087
You probably was.

01:28.088 --> 01:30.158
By what?

01:31.225 --> 01:34.395
There's a whole town
underneath us.

01:34.395 --> 01:36.864
The hell out of here, man.

01:36.897 --> 01:39.400
That's what I'm saying.

01:39.400 --> 01:41.569
Shit water.

01:41.569 --> 01:44.071
This whole lake
used to be a town.

01:44.071 --> 01:46.073
Houses, barns, roads.

01:46.073 --> 01:48.242
There's a whole raceway
down there.

01:48.242 --> 01:51.279
State government built a dam
and flooded the place.

01:51.345 --> 01:53.614
Anyone who didn't leave drowned.

01:56.284 --> 01:59.086
Town was Black, too.

01:59.119 --> 02:00.354
What?

02:01.422 --> 02:03.891
Self-governed Black town.

02:07.528 --> 02:11.131
So, there are Black people
under us right now?

02:12.800 --> 02:14.802
Yeah. Why you think
so many people die

02:14.868 --> 02:16.437
around here every year?

02:18.038 --> 02:20.274
'Cause of drunk rednecks
trying to fish at night.

02:20.274 --> 02:21.775
Like you.

02:26.380 --> 02:27.981
No.

02:28.048 --> 02:30.618
It's 'cause it's haunted.

02:35.556 --> 02:37.625
You-you really think
it's haunted?

02:37.625 --> 02:40.461
Oh, yeah.

02:40.494 --> 02:43.497
Lot of souls down there.

02:43.564 --> 02:45.633
That's what pulled you under.

02:45.666 --> 02:47.435
Town full of Black folk.

02:47.468 --> 02:50.170
They were almost white.

02:50.238 --> 02:52.406
Get the hell out of here, man.
What are you talking about?

02:53.474 --> 02:55.409
They were almost white?

02:56.510 --> 02:58.746
White's not a real thing, right?

03:00.481 --> 03:03.684
There's no scientific basis
for it.

03:03.751 --> 03:07.187
People just... become white.

03:07.255 --> 03:09.089
It's social.

03:12.092 --> 03:14.995
White is where you are.

03:14.995 --> 03:17.265
It's when you are.

03:18.266 --> 03:21.769
Armenians are white as hell
till they ain't.

03:23.937 --> 03:25.873
Armenians?

03:28.208 --> 03:30.844
When they dammed
the Chattahoochee,

03:30.844 --> 03:33.013
some refused to leave.

03:34.715 --> 03:36.784
They thought they were safe.

03:38.386 --> 03:41.722
They'd paid to be white.

03:43.056 --> 03:46.059
With enough blood and money,
anyone can be white.

03:47.861 --> 03:49.730
It's always been that way.

03:52.199 --> 03:56.069
But the thing about
being white is

03:56.136 --> 03:57.905
it blinds you.

03:59.873 --> 04:02.042
It's easy to see
the Black man as cursed

04:02.075 --> 04:05.546
because you've separated
yourself from him.

04:06.547 --> 04:09.717
But you don't know...

04:09.717 --> 04:12.420
you're enslaved just like him.

04:14.254 --> 04:17.658
Cold whiteness.

04:19.259 --> 04:21.729
You're hypothermic.

04:21.729 --> 04:24.097
You lose logic.

04:25.566 --> 04:27.568
You see the blood...

04:29.337 --> 04:32.239
...and you think
someone else is bleeding.

04:34.575 --> 04:40.247
Everyone is screaming at you
to turn the machine off,

04:40.247 --> 04:42.249
but you can't hear them.

04:43.917 --> 04:47.388
You can't even
hear yourself saying,

04:47.421 --> 04:49.423
- "We're cursed, too."

04:51.124 --> 04:52.593
We're cursed, too!

04:52.626 --> 04:56.430
Oh, shit!

05:02.770 --> 05:05.272
I don't want to keep
reminding you about this.

05:05.305 --> 05:07.074
- Oh, and one more thing
before we go.

05:07.107 --> 05:08.742
- Listen up, everyone.

05:08.776 --> 05:11.412
I have a special announcement
to make.

05:11.445 --> 05:13.414
In an effort
to promote more Black history

05:13.447 --> 05:16.417
in the curriculum,
our school has partnered up

05:16.450 --> 05:19.252
with the Atlanta Falcons
and Domino's Pizza

05:19.286 --> 05:20.788
for the
Change Atlanta Initiative.

05:20.821 --> 05:25.092
So, next Thursday,
we're all going on a field trip.

05:25.125 --> 05:27.728
We're all going
to go watch a movie.

05:29.397 --> 05:31.465
The new Black Panther 2.

05:31.499 --> 05:33.801
- Let's go!
- I know. Okay.

05:33.834 --> 05:35.335
I know. It's exciting...

05:35.403 --> 05:37.137
- Oh.
- Loquareeous.

05:37.170 --> 05:39.640
Hey! Hey! Hey!

05:39.640 --> 05:41.675
- Loquareeous, sit down!
- Hey! Hey!

05:41.742 --> 05:43.276
- Loquareeous!

05:43.310 --> 05:45.145
Loquareeous, sit down right now!

05:46.414 --> 05:47.781
Hey! Hey!

05:47.815 --> 05:50.918
Loquareeous, sit down right now,
young man!

05:53.687 --> 05:54.955
Hi, Mom.

05:54.988 --> 05:56.990
Please. Come in and have a seat.

05:57.024 --> 05:58.826
Mm-hmm.

05:58.826 --> 06:00.661
How's everyone doing today?

06:00.694 --> 06:02.696
First of all,

06:02.763 --> 06:05.633
I done already told y'all
to stop calling me down here.

06:05.666 --> 06:08.502
Well, I really appreciate you
coming down, Ms. Reid.

06:08.536 --> 06:11.672
And you're Loquareeous's
grandfather, right?

06:11.705 --> 06:13.674
Thank you both for coming.

06:13.707 --> 06:16.844
As you know,
there was a disruption

06:16.877 --> 06:19.346
- with Loquareeous...
- Uh, let me jump in here.

06:19.379 --> 06:22.015
Sorry. Uh, I'm the guidance
counselor, Mrs. Grier.

06:22.015 --> 06:25.352
Let me start by saying
I am a big fan of your son.

06:25.385 --> 06:27.354
He's been
to my office a few times

06:27.387 --> 06:29.356
already this semester
for disciplinary problems--

06:29.389 --> 06:30.858
talking in class,
being disruptive...

06:30.891 --> 06:33.694
- Well, then give him detention.
- Well, yes.

06:33.727 --> 06:36.063
He's-he's had detention before.

06:36.129 --> 06:37.698
Several times.

06:37.731 --> 06:39.366
But I-I had a thought.

06:39.399 --> 06:41.401
Maybe the reason that he's being
disruptive in class

06:41.469 --> 06:43.036
is because the material
is too challenging.

06:43.070 --> 06:44.538
If we put him in remedial math

06:44.538 --> 06:45.873
and language arts,
he could have the...

06:45.906 --> 06:47.708
Wait. Wait.

06:47.741 --> 06:49.877
What? No.

06:49.877 --> 06:53.013
- My son is not dumb.
- Oh, no, no.

06:53.046 --> 06:55.182
He's an idiot.
Y'all ridiculous.

06:55.215 --> 06:57.050
He is not the first kid
to act up in class,

06:57.050 --> 06:58.919
and you want to push him back
some grades?

06:58.986 --> 07:00.387
No, I just thought
it could be...

07:00.420 --> 07:02.055
Don't you move my son.

07:02.055 --> 07:04.692
Tell his teachers
to give him detention.

07:04.725 --> 07:07.728
- Thank you for coming.
- Mm-hmm.

07:09.563 --> 07:12.065
Okay, that went very well.

07:12.065 --> 07:15.268
I thought I... I-I think
he could really use the...

07:15.335 --> 07:16.737
Ms. Reid?

07:16.770 --> 07:18.405
- I'm sorry.

07:18.438 --> 07:20.708
Uh-uh! You better dance!

07:20.741 --> 07:22.710
Since you love to dance so much,
go 'head.

07:22.743 --> 07:25.078
Shoot it. Come on, shoot!

07:25.112 --> 07:27.380
You got these people up here
thinking you retarded.

07:27.414 --> 07:30.083
Your ass gonna end up
in them SPED classes.

07:30.083 --> 07:31.552
Now whip.

07:31.585 --> 07:33.120
Mm-hmm.

07:33.186 --> 07:34.588
Nae Nae. Come on.

07:34.588 --> 07:37.424
Ay. Ay. Ay.

07:37.424 --> 07:39.760
Hit it. Hit it!

07:42.195 --> 07:44.097
If you don't start using your
common sense and acting right,

07:44.097 --> 07:45.633
these white people--
they gon' kill you.

07:45.699 --> 07:48.435
- Ms. Reid, d...
- Kill... you.

07:48.435 --> 07:50.137
- Now do the worm.
- Really,
there's no need for that.

07:50.203 --> 07:51.872
- Let's see it.
- There's no need for that.

07:55.543 --> 07:57.811
You up here showing out
for your white classmates.

07:57.878 --> 07:59.446
Yeah,
you laughing with them now,

07:59.479 --> 08:01.314
but they're gonna be
the only ones laughing

08:01.381 --> 08:03.617
when you dead or in jail.

08:05.619 --> 08:07.254
I wasn't even trying
to show out...

08:07.287 --> 08:09.122
I don't want to hear it!

08:18.899 --> 08:21.635
- What's your problem?
- Now get to class.

08:21.669 --> 08:24.504
And I better not get
another call from this school.

08:24.572 --> 08:26.807
I'll walk him back.

08:28.809 --> 08:30.343
Don't worry.

08:30.410 --> 08:32.646
I'm gonna get you out of there.

08:45.092 --> 08:47.661
Mom, there ain't no more milk!

08:47.695 --> 08:51.699
There's spaghetti in
the refrigerator if you hungry.

09:05.946 --> 09:08.816
You better not be
watching that TV.

09:08.849 --> 09:10.851
I'm-a check, and I'll know.

09:22.029 --> 09:23.731
Hello. Ms. Reid, right?

09:23.797 --> 09:25.699
Who wants to know?

09:25.733 --> 09:28.168
I'm with Family
and Children's Services.

09:28.201 --> 09:30.170
I'm here on behalf of the city
to conduct a welfare ch...

09:30.203 --> 09:32.873
- Family and Children's Services?
- Yes, ma'am.

09:32.906 --> 09:35.408
I'm here to conduct
a welfare check on your son...

09:35.475 --> 09:37.410
- Loqua...
- Loquareeous!

09:37.477 --> 09:39.880
- Oh, yes.
- Uh-huh.
- Get in here!

09:39.913 --> 09:43.383
- See, y'all got me fucked up.
- Oh, ma'am, I just need a few

09:43.416 --> 09:45.552
- moments to speak with you.
- Did you call the police on me?

09:45.552 --> 09:47.721
- No.
- Oh, Ms. Reid,

09:47.721 --> 09:49.089
the police are just here
as a precaution.

09:49.156 --> 09:51.058
Take him.

09:51.091 --> 09:52.926
Go ahead.

09:52.993 --> 09:54.895
- Ma.
- Since you want
to go so bad, bye.

09:54.895 --> 09:56.730
Ma, I didn't call nobody.

09:56.730 --> 09:59.232
- You know what?
- Wait.

09:59.232 --> 10:00.768
Mom.

10:02.736 --> 10:05.238
Mama, I didn't call nobody.

10:05.272 --> 10:07.775
I ain't giving you
all these clothes that I bought.

10:07.841 --> 10:09.409
Y'all better take this boy

10:09.442 --> 10:11.111
- Before I kill him...
- Mom.

10:11.178 --> 10:14.581
- ...and he got a real reason
to call the police.

10:14.581 --> 10:15.883
Mom.

10:15.916 --> 10:17.250
Mama, wait!

11:02.662 --> 11:04.798
Oh, my goodness.

11:09.302 --> 11:11.438
Welcome home, son. Okay.

11:11.471 --> 11:13.106
Quickly, get inside.

11:13.140 --> 11:14.975
Thank you so much
for doing this last minute.

11:14.975 --> 11:16.844
We always appreciate it, Amber.

11:16.910 --> 11:18.445
Oh, it's not a problem at all.

11:18.478 --> 11:20.147
It's what we do.

11:20.180 --> 11:22.282
All right, well,
let's get you settled.

11:22.315 --> 11:26.820
I am Amber,
but you can call me "Mom."

11:26.854 --> 11:29.289
Um, oh, those are
your new brothers and sisters.

11:29.322 --> 11:33.160
That's Lanre, Yves and Fatima.

11:34.161 --> 11:36.663
Ugh. It's stinky here.

11:36.696 --> 11:39.332
Oh, no, no, no,
it doesn't stink.

11:39.332 --> 11:41.634
Come on, this way.

11:41.668 --> 11:44.171
We've kind of turned our kitchen
into a workshop.

11:44.204 --> 11:46.639
We're trying to make
an olive oil shampoo,

11:46.673 --> 11:49.843
and we started mixing together
some African Dudu soap.

11:49.843 --> 11:52.479
It's not what it sounds like.

11:52.512 --> 11:55.348
We make our own kombucha.
Yummy, huh?

11:55.382 --> 11:59.686
And we pickle our own veggies
using our organic garden.

11:59.719 --> 12:01.822
Um, we're selling it
at the farmers market tomorrow.

12:01.855 --> 12:04.024
You're gonna love it.

12:04.057 --> 12:06.393
Oh, um, and that is
your other mom.

12:06.459 --> 12:08.661
And that little guy is Cornpop.

12:08.695 --> 12:10.397
Welcome to the family.

12:13.400 --> 12:15.702
So do I call you both "Mom"?

12:15.735 --> 12:18.571
- Yes.
- Call me Gayle.

12:20.908 --> 12:23.710
Oh, dinner's at 5:30,
so wash up first.

12:23.710 --> 12:25.879
Um, we're having fried chicken.

12:25.879 --> 12:28.548
And, um, since it's your first
night, I'll let you decide.

12:28.581 --> 12:30.717
Do you want capers or sprouts?

12:30.717 --> 12:32.552
I don't know what that is.

12:32.552 --> 12:34.554
- Aw.

12:34.554 --> 12:36.556
Capers it is.

12:36.589 --> 12:39.226
- Oh, will you get me
that chicken over there?
- Mm. Mm.

12:43.263 --> 12:44.898
Perfect.

12:47.835 --> 12:49.736
Uh, how much
did we do it last time?

12:49.736 --> 12:51.571
- 12 minutes is too long, right?
- Yeah.

12:51.571 --> 12:54.574
- It was a little dry.
- Okay, let's do
eight and a half, then.

12:54.574 --> 12:55.775
Mm-hmm.

13:19.432 --> 13:20.868
Hey.

13:22.102 --> 13:25.372
I just wanted to see
that you were settled in.

13:28.775 --> 13:32.479
I made you something special
for your first day.

13:37.284 --> 13:39.152
This says "Larry."

13:39.219 --> 13:42.622
Oh, well, I didn't know
how to spell "Loo-Kway-reeous,"

13:42.655 --> 13:44.624
so I figured
we'd call you "Larry."

13:44.657 --> 13:48.295
Larry's a great nickname. Hmm.

13:48.328 --> 13:50.497
Um, where's the washcloth?

13:52.632 --> 13:55.002
It's okay. He's new here.

13:55.068 --> 13:58.471
You just use your hands.

13:58.471 --> 14:00.007
Even on my butt?

14:01.008 --> 14:03.944
Oh, we need to take a picture.

14:03.977 --> 14:05.478
Get around.

14:06.980 --> 14:08.916
Get the towel.
Get the towel.

14:10.150 --> 14:12.119
- Okay.

14:12.152 --> 14:13.987
Perfect!

14:22.162 --> 14:23.496
What are you wearing?

14:23.530 --> 14:25.165
Pajamas.

14:25.165 --> 14:26.666
You can wear that tonight,

14:26.699 --> 14:28.868
but from now,
I'll lay your clothes out.

14:32.205 --> 14:35.175
You can sprinkle
some rosemary on it if you want.

14:35.208 --> 14:37.677
Mm-mm. Mmm. It's great.

14:37.677 --> 14:39.112
Mmm.

14:42.015 --> 14:43.516
Larry, you're not eating.

14:43.550 --> 14:45.518
This food is nasty.

14:45.552 --> 14:47.354
If I eat it, I'll throw up.

14:47.354 --> 14:51.191
Larry, we do not say
"throw up" at the table.

14:51.224 --> 14:53.026
But it's nasty.

14:53.060 --> 14:56.696
No, honey.
It's just better for you.

14:56.729 --> 14:59.566
There's too much salt and oil
in most of the foods

14:59.632 --> 15:01.534
that you're used to.

15:03.870 --> 15:06.206
Oh, did you see
on Instagram today

15:06.239 --> 15:09.209
that Rihanna used the phrase
"spirit animal"?

15:09.209 --> 15:10.577
No. Please.

15:10.643 --> 15:12.712
Please tell me that Rihanna
is an indigenous person

15:12.712 --> 15:14.247
- and I just don't know it.
- Uh-uh.

15:15.983 --> 15:18.986
Oh, my God. We got to comment
on that, right?

15:23.890 --> 15:25.425
Mm.

15:32.165 --> 15:33.733
Hello.

15:33.766 --> 15:35.102
This is she.

15:35.168 --> 15:37.237
We're having dinner.

16:02.695 --> 16:04.797
I don't understand
why the bill collectors

16:04.864 --> 16:06.566
are always
just calling during dinner.

16:06.599 --> 16:09.302
- I put us on that
"do not call" list.
- Well, they're calling.

16:09.369 --> 16:10.737
This food is nasty!

16:10.770 --> 16:12.939
Larry, we don't...

16:13.940 --> 16:15.442
You want to know something?

16:16.943 --> 16:19.479
There are starving children
in Africa.

16:19.546 --> 16:21.281
You don't believe me,
ask your brother.

16:22.949 --> 16:24.451
I want a hamburger.

16:24.484 --> 16:26.486
- We don't have hamburgers.

16:26.553 --> 16:27.954
That's what the dog is eating.

16:28.888 --> 16:30.990
- Well, yeah,
that's Cornpop's food.

16:31.058 --> 16:33.626
You don't..? Okay, you don't
want to eat, you can go to bed.

16:33.660 --> 16:35.795
- It's 6:00!
- Okay.

16:35.795 --> 16:38.131
- Man, I hate this house!

16:38.165 --> 16:40.300
We don't use the word
"hate" in this house.

16:40.300 --> 16:42.335
Hate, hate, hate, hate,
hate, hate, hate, hate!

17:19.038 --> 17:21.508
So, this is the last

17:21.541 --> 17:23.610
that Marcos can give us
on credit.

17:25.011 --> 17:29.349
Hey. We're gonna have to make
some more adjustments.

17:36.889 --> 17:38.358
We didn't eat lunch.

17:38.358 --> 17:42.061
You had celery and carrots,
remember?

17:42.129 --> 17:43.363
I'm still hungry.

17:43.396 --> 17:45.365
You're supposed to be hungry.

17:45.398 --> 17:47.967
If you're full,
that means you ate too much.

17:52.705 --> 17:55.074
How much longer
do we have to do this?

17:56.042 --> 17:58.211
Why don't you try
singing a song while you work?

17:58.211 --> 17:59.879
It might make you feel better.

18:06.919 --> 18:09.389
Sing something silly,
like, um...

18:24.404 --> 18:26.739
Okay, back to work, Larry.

18:26.739 --> 18:30.076
We got to leave for the
farmers market in 30 minutes.

18:40.853 --> 18:43.790
Oh, your family's so cute.

18:43.856 --> 18:47.059
Oh, thank you so much.

18:47.093 --> 18:49.061
Larry,
can you put some effort in?

18:49.095 --> 18:51.531
Shake your booty. Come on.

18:52.532 --> 18:55.134
Aw. Is Hugs your father?

18:56.869 --> 18:58.104
No.

19:05.278 --> 19:07.614
- Larry.
- Whoa. Oh.

19:12.785 --> 19:14.654
- Whoa! Kid, I almost shot you!
- I learned my lesson.

19:14.721 --> 19:16.923
I hate my new parents.
They can't cook,

19:16.956 --> 19:18.758
- and they make me sleep
in a storage closet.
- All right.

19:18.791 --> 19:21.661
Slow down.
Y... Your parents did this?

19:21.728 --> 19:24.096
My moms.
They make me do all the chores,

19:24.130 --> 19:26.499
and I didn't eat nothing.
Please take me home.

19:26.566 --> 19:28.501
- I'm tired
of these white ladies.
- All right, calm down.

19:28.568 --> 19:29.802
- I don't know
what you're talking...
- Excuse me, Officer.

19:29.836 --> 19:31.170
Is there a problem?

19:31.238 --> 19:33.640
Um, that's our son.

19:34.574 --> 19:36.142
- This is your son?
- Yes.

19:36.175 --> 19:39.846
Yeah. My wife, Amber and I--
we adopt impoverished children.

19:39.912 --> 19:41.848
We have a kombucha stand
right over there.

19:41.914 --> 19:43.750
Did you want some?

19:45.084 --> 19:48.020
Oh. I see what's going on.

19:48.087 --> 19:50.357
Okay. I think
he's just tired is all.

19:50.423 --> 19:51.991
He said he wanted to go home.

19:51.991 --> 19:53.493
Maybe he thought I'd arrest you

19:53.493 --> 19:55.462
for not letting him
play PlayStation.

19:55.495 --> 19:57.364
- Uh, well,

19:57.430 --> 19:59.532
all four of our children
are Black, so we always

19:59.599 --> 20:02.335
make sure to tell them that
the police are their friends.

20:02.369 --> 20:04.003
Yeah.

20:05.605 --> 20:07.674
- Come on.
- Hey.

20:07.674 --> 20:11.177
You know who he reminds me of
in that hat?

20:11.210 --> 20:12.679
Aloe Blacc.

20:12.712 --> 20:14.847
- Yes. Exactly.
- Yeah.

20:14.847 --> 20:17.517
- Thank you so much.

20:17.550 --> 20:19.552
- Come on.
- Come on.

20:28.227 --> 20:31.163
Larry, you are helping so much.
I'm so proud of you.

20:31.197 --> 20:33.032
I didn't say that shit!

20:36.369 --> 20:39.071
I know being here
isn't easy for you...

20:40.640 --> 20:44.711
...but I am gonna love that
right out of you.

20:44.711 --> 20:46.379
I promise.

20:54.387 --> 20:56.389
You know, where you come from,

20:56.389 --> 20:58.858
they have a name
for what you are.

20:58.891 --> 21:01.060
What?

21:01.060 --> 21:03.062
A snitch.

21:06.899 --> 21:10.403
We all have to work hard
to keep this family together.

21:12.339 --> 21:14.441
And I'm sure this is
a much better situation

21:14.507 --> 21:16.409
than where you came from.

21:19.946 --> 21:21.448
Goddamn it.

21:29.589 --> 21:31.257
May I help you?

21:31.257 --> 21:33.393
Hi. I'm with
Family and Children's Services.

21:33.426 --> 21:34.927
We got a call
from one of your neighbors

21:34.961 --> 21:37.430
and would like to do
a wellness check on the kids.

21:39.265 --> 21:40.700
Mm-hmm.

21:43.302 --> 21:45.938
- May I come in?
- Mm.

21:52.812 --> 21:54.781
Look, if it was
Chris Meyers next door,

21:54.814 --> 21:56.783
I mean, you can't really believe
anything that he says.

21:56.783 --> 21:59.318
- He's, like, one of those
Bernie Bro women-haters.
- Excuse me.

21:59.386 --> 22:01.654
What is that smell?

22:01.721 --> 22:03.155
Uh, kombucha.

22:03.222 --> 22:04.824
Pickled brussels sprouts.

22:04.891 --> 22:06.125
Both.

22:08.561 --> 22:10.963
So, I was going over your file,
and I noticed

22:10.997 --> 22:13.299
- that you moved here
five months ago.
- Mm-hmm.

22:13.299 --> 22:15.301
But when I called
Bledsoe County,

22:15.301 --> 22:17.970
they said that they could not
locate a record.

22:18.004 --> 22:20.006
Well, normally,
Kasey's our caseworker.

22:20.072 --> 22:21.674
Did something happen?

22:21.741 --> 22:23.510
She's sick.

22:23.576 --> 22:25.011
There is dog hair

22:25.077 --> 22:27.346
- everywhere in here.

22:30.082 --> 22:31.984
Hello, darling.

22:31.984 --> 22:33.820
Are you feeling okay?

22:35.154 --> 22:37.123
Oh.

22:37.156 --> 22:39.325
What is this?

22:39.358 --> 22:41.661
Blueberries, like medicine.

22:42.662 --> 22:45.364
Okay. Do you have
a washcloth I can use?

22:46.999 --> 22:49.001
Uh, no.

23:04.050 --> 23:06.052
So how do you like living here?

23:08.555 --> 23:10.990
I'm really, really hungry.

23:11.023 --> 23:12.525
I just want to go home.

23:13.560 --> 23:16.529
Don't worry.
I'm gonna get you out of here.

23:16.563 --> 23:19.031
Um, you know, could I speak
with you privately?

23:19.065 --> 23:21.167
I just think that there's
some things about our case

23:21.200 --> 23:22.702
you don't... you don't know.

23:22.735 --> 23:25.204
- Um, sure. That's fine.
- We'll go here.

23:25.204 --> 23:26.739
Amber, why don't you
start dinner.

23:26.806 --> 23:27.874
Larry's hungry.

23:50.897 --> 23:52.599
Everything's fine.

23:56.068 --> 23:58.738
- We're good.
- Well, that's fantastic.

23:58.738 --> 24:00.573
I made fried chicken again.

24:05.277 --> 24:06.913
Eat up, guys.

24:28.701 --> 24:30.269
If you don't start using

24:30.302 --> 24:31.771
your common sense
and acting right,

24:31.771 --> 24:33.973
these white people--
they gon' kill you.

24:34.040 --> 24:36.475
Kill you!

25:03.570 --> 25:05.572
What's your problem?

25:45.044 --> 25:47.013
Amber?

25:47.046 --> 25:48.514
Oh. Hey, Larry.

25:48.514 --> 25:49.849
Oh, we're going
to the Grand Canyon.

25:49.882 --> 25:51.117
You should get dressed.

25:52.184 --> 25:53.519
Grand Canyon?

25:53.552 --> 25:55.888
Yeah. It's gonna be fun.

26:03.395 --> 26:05.698
Where are we going? Really.

26:08.034 --> 26:09.702
Larry, get dressed.

26:09.702 --> 26:12.238
We got to get going
before the sun goes down.

26:16.876 --> 26:18.911
Okay. Let's go, guys.

26:29.822 --> 26:31.357
Larry?

26:31.390 --> 26:33.159
Come on. Let's go.

28:11.858 --> 28:13.359
Okay, Cornpop.

28:15.594 --> 28:17.329
Go be free.

28:18.364 --> 28:19.832
Go.

28:29.108 --> 28:32.311
Hey, Cornpop's a survivor, okay?

28:32.344 --> 28:33.679
He's-he's gonna make it.

28:33.712 --> 28:36.215
Someone's gonna
take care of him.

28:36.282 --> 28:38.684
What the hell are we doing?

28:39.718 --> 28:42.021
Well, we're doing
what needs to be done.

28:44.023 --> 28:47.193
You know the world
we live in, Amber.

28:47.226 --> 28:49.728
It's horrible for these kids.

28:49.796 --> 28:52.698
Without us to protect them,
what's gonna happen to them?

28:52.731 --> 28:54.867
They're gonna go back
into foster care.

28:54.867 --> 28:57.369
Just release them in the wild
like Cornpop?

28:57.369 --> 28:59.371
We'd be prolonging
the inevitable.

29:05.544 --> 29:08.414
Uh, when we adopted Fatima,

29:08.480 --> 29:10.416
I knew we were doing
the right thing.

29:10.482 --> 29:13.552
The agency even said so.

29:13.552 --> 29:15.554
I mean, we got that big loan
from the bank.

29:15.554 --> 29:17.890
I thought that... I thought
that meant we were solid.

29:19.558 --> 29:21.260
Everyone was so supportive.

29:21.327 --> 29:23.562
Every single person.

29:25.731 --> 29:27.934
And I just kept thinking,
"Why...

29:28.000 --> 29:30.502
Why isn't anyone stopping us?"

29:33.772 --> 29:36.742
Why didn't anyone stop us,
Gayle?

30:01.200 --> 30:03.435
I... I don't think
I can do this.

30:10.709 --> 30:12.278
Don't look back.

31:41.200 --> 31:43.202
Larry!

33:30.342 --> 33:32.911
So you finally decided
to come home, huh?

33:37.249 --> 33:39.185
Wait, Mom.

33:39.251 --> 33:40.652
Yeah, baby?

33:42.654 --> 33:44.656
Some spaghetti in there?

33:48.360 --> 33:50.262
Yeah, spaghetti in there.

33:56.535 --> 33:59.037
Shocking news tonight.

33:59.105 --> 34:01.840
Authorities found children
at a rest stop,

34:01.840 --> 34:04.843
apparently abandoned
after their adoptive parents

34:04.843 --> 34:07.846
committed suicide
by driving off of a bridge...

34:11.717 --> 34:14.353
Terrible story.
